{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PL7VrtNi76PqsoZzynwgxt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd105-stty\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/stty: Change and Print Terminal Line Settings\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD stty that differs from GNU stty in output format and flag naming.\n6\t  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gstty, installed\n7\t  by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential testing\n8\t  via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Print and change terminal line settings.\n12\t  - G2: Support all standard control characters, input/output/local/control mode flags.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gstty via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default display\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print a summary of current terminal settings (speed, line discipline, changed-from-default settings) matching GNU stty output format.\n21\t\n22\t  R2:\n23\t    title: All settings display\n24\t    items:\n25\t      - R2.1:\n26\t          text: \"-a or --all must print all current terminal settings in a human-readable format.\"\n27\t\n28\t  R3:\n29\t    title: Save/restore and device\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R3.1:\n32\t          text: \"-g or --save must print all current terminal settings in a machine-readable format (stty-readable) that can be passed back as arguments to restore settings.\"\n33\t      - R3.2:\n34\t          text: \"-F DEVICE or --file=DEVICE must operate on the specified terminal device instead of stdin.\"\n35\t\n36\t  R4:\n37\t    title: Change settings\n38\t    items:\n39\t      - R4.1:\n40\t          text: \"Must accept setting names as arguments to enable them, and names prefixed with - to disable them (e.g., stty -echo disables echo, stty echo enables it).\"\n41\t\n42\t  R5:\n43\t    title: Special characters\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R5.1:\n46\t          text: \"Must support special characters: intr, quit, erase, kill, eof, eol, eol2, swtch, start, stop, susp, rprnt, werase, lnext, discard, min, time.\"\n47\t\n48\t  R6:\n49\t    title: Combination and speed settings\n50\t    items:\n51\t      - R6.1:\n52\t          text: \"Must support combination settings: sane (reset to reasonable defaults), cooked (same as -raw), raw (set raw mode), evenp/parity (set even parity), oddp (set odd parity).\"\n53\t      - R6.2:\n54\t          text: \"Must support speed setting: ispeed N, ospeed N, or N alone to set both input and output speed.\"\n55\t\n56\t  R7:\n57\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n58\t    items:\n59\t      - R7.1:\n60\t          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n61\t      - R7.2:\n62\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error (invalid setting, cannot open device).\n63\t      - R7.3:\n64\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n65\t\n66\tnon_goals:\n67\t  - cmd/stty does not implement all obscure termios flags; it covers the commonly used set matching GNU stty output.\n68\t\n69\tacceptance_criteria:\n70\t  - id: AC1\n71\t    criterion: \"stty with no arguments prints terminal settings summary, matching gstty.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t  - id: AC2\n75\t    criterion: \"stty -a prints all settings, matching gstty -a.\"\n76\t    traces:\n77\t      - R2.1\n78\t  - id: AC3\n79\t    criterion: \"stty -g prints machine-readable settings, matching gstty -g.\"\n80\t    traces:\n81\t      - R3.1\n82\t  - id: AC4\n83\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gstty passes.\"\n84\t    traces:\n85\t      - R1.1\n86\t      - R2.1\n87\t      - R3.1\n88\t  - id: AC5\n89\t    criterion: \"cmd/stty compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n90\t    traces:\n91\t      - R1.1\n92\t      - R2.1\n93\t      - R3.1\n94\t      - R3.2\n95\t      - R4.1\n96\t      - R5.1\n97\t      - R6.1\n98\t      - R6.2\n99\t      - R7.1\n100\t      - R7.2\n101\t      - R7.3\n102\t\n103\tpackage_contract:\n104\t  imports:\n105\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n106\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4766f4dd-6cc1-473e-8675-aaab6bf559a6","uuid":"c1858516-cb01-4202-ad89-ee266af4d1cc","timestamp":"2026-05-28T19:20:02.423Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd105-stty.yaml","content":"id: srd105-stty\ntitle: \"cmd/stty: Change and Print Terminal Line Settings\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD stty that differs from GNU stty in output format and flag naming.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gstty, installed\n  by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential testing\n  via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print and change terminal line settings.\n  - G2: Support all standard control characters, input/output/local/control mode flags.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gstty via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default display\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print a summary of current terminal settings (speed, line discipline, changed-from-default settings) matching GNU stty output format.\n\n  R2:\n    title: All settings display\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-a or --all must print all current terminal settings in a human-readable format.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Save/restore and device\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-g or --save must print all current terminal settings in a machine-readable format (stty-readable) that can be passed back as arguments to restore settings.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-F DEVICE or --file=DEVICE must operate on the specified terminal device instead of stdin.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Change settings\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: \"Must accept setting names as arguments to enable them, and names prefixed with - to disable them (e.g., stty -echo disables echo, stty echo enables it).\"\n\n  R5:\n    title: Special characters\n    items:\n      - R5.1:\n          text: \"Must support special characters: intr, quit, erase, kill, eof, eol, eol2, swtch, start, stop, susp, rprnt, werase, lnext, discard, min, time.\"\n\n  R6:\n    title: Combination and speed settings\n    items:\n      - R6.1:\n          text: \"Must support combination settings: sane (reset to reasonable defaults), cooked (same as -raw), raw (set raw mode), evenp/parity (set even parity), oddp (set odd parity).\"\n      - R6.2:\n          text: \"Must support speed setting: ispeed N, ospeed N, or N alone to set both input and output speed.\"\n\n  R7:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R7.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n      - R7.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on any error (invalid setting, cannot open device).\n      - R7.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/stty does not implement all obscure termios flags; it covers the commonly used set matching GNU stty output.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"stty with no arguments prints terminal settings summary, matching gstty.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"stty -a prints all settings, matching gstty -a.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"stty -g prints machine-readable settings, matching gstty -g.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gstty passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/stty compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R5.1\n      - R6.1\n      - R6.2\n      - R7.1\n      - R7.2\n      - R7.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":106,"startLine":1,"totalLines":106}}}
