{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017DZa1h8BPZYtEKkEsQqRUP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd052-tty\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/tty: Print Terminal File Name\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Scripts use tty to determine whether stdin is connected to a terminal and to obtain the\n6\t  terminal device name. The -s (silent) flag suppresses output and reports only via exit\n7\t  code, which is useful in conditional expressions. The Go implementation must match the\n8\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtty, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout\n9\t  and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the file name of the terminal connected to stdin.\n13\t  - G2: Support the -s (silent) flag for exit-code-only operation.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default behavior and silent mode\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments and stdin is a terminal, must print the terminal device name (e.g., /dev/ttys000) followed by a newline and exit 0.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: When invoked with no arguments and stdin is not a terminal, must print \"not a tty\" followed by a newline and exit 1.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"-s (--silent, --quiet) must suppress all output. The exit code is 0 if stdin is a terminal, 1 otherwise.\"\n25\t\n26\t  R2:\n27\t    title: Error handling\n28\t    items:\n29\t      - R2.1:\n30\t          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 2.\n31\t      - R2.2:\n32\t          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 2.\n33\t\n34\t  R3:\n35\t    title: Differential testing\n36\t    items:\n37\t      - R3.1:\n38\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gtty) via pkg/testutils.\n39\t      - R3.2:\n40\t          text: \"Tests must cover: stdin connected to a terminal (if available), stdin redirected from a file or pipe (not a tty), -s flag, and error cases.\"\n41\t      - R3.3:\n42\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n43\t\n44\tnon_goals:\n45\t  - cmd/tty does not configure terminal settings; use stty for that.\n46\t  - cmd/tty does not check terminals connected to stdout or stderr; it checks stdin only.\n47\t\n48\tacceptance_criteria:\n49\t  - id: AC1\n50\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/tty with stdin from a pipe prints \\\"not a tty\\\" and exits 1, matching gtty.\"\n51\t    traces:\n52\t      - R1.1\n53\t      - R1.2\n54\t      - R1.3\n55\t      - R2.1\n56\t      - R2.2\n57\t      - R3.1\n58\t      - R3.2\n59\t  - id: AC2\n60\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/tty -s with stdin from a pipe produces no output and exits 1, matching gtty.\"\n61\t    traces:\n62\t      - R1.1\n63\t      - R1.2\n64\t      - R1.3\n65\t      - R2.1\n66\t      - R2.2\n67\t      - R3.1\n68\t      - R3.2\n69\t  - id: AC3\n70\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtty passes for piped and terminal stdin cases.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.1\n73\t      - R1.2\n74\t      - R1.3\n75\t      - R3.1\n76\t      - R3.2\n77\t      - R3.3\n78\t  - id: AC4\n79\t    criterion: \"cmd/tty compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n80\t    traces:\n81\t      - R1.1\n82\t      - R1.2\n83\t      - R1.3\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R3.1\n87\t      - R3.2\n88\t      - R3.3\n89\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BwpTYm5bvMN9bbibU2HZ3B","session_id":"4766f4dd-6cc1-473e-8675-aaab6bf559a6","uuid":"4563fb5b-aba2-4cba-9dfc-a3c8c3a3454b","timestamp":"2026-05-28T19:21:13.280Z"}
