{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NfzKq1tj6f4igzDgkb41bp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: rel15.0-uc002-stty\n2\ttitle: \"Change terminal settings via stty\"\n3\t\n4\tsummary: |\n5\t  The operator runs the Go stty binary. The differential testing harness runs both\n6\t  the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gstty from coreutils) with identical\n7\t  inputs and confirms behavior parity.\n8\t\n9\tactor: Human Operator\n10\t\n11\ttrigger: |\n12\t  The operator has completed the PRD (srd105-stty.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n13\t  a passing differential test for cmd/stty.\n14\t\n15\tflow:\n16\t  - id: F1\n17\t    step: |\n18\t      The operator exercises stty with standard flag combinations and inputs.\n19\t  - id: F2\n20\t    step: |\n21\t      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/stty and\n22\t      gstty with the same inputs and compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes.\n23\t\n24\ttouchpoints:\n25\t  - T1: \"cmd/stty — stty prints and changes terminal settings (srd105-stty R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6, R7)\"\n26\t  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and comparison\"\n27\t  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n28\t\n29\tsuccess_criteria:\n30\t  - id: S1\n31\t    criterion: |\n32\t      The differential test passes for all standard flag combinations, confirming\n33\t      full parity with gstty.\n34\t    traces:\n35\t      - AC1\n36\t\n37\tout_of_scope:\n38\t  - Platform-specific features not available on macOS.\n39\t\n40\ttest_suite: test-rel15.0\n41\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_