{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BwpTYm5bvMN9bbibU2HZ3B","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create the final report:\n\n## Summary Report: Termios-Related Code and cmd/ Implementation Patterns\n\n### Termios-Related Code and Files\n\n**No existing cmd implementations use termios directly yet.** However, termios support is planned:\n\n1. **Planned stty implementation**\n   - File: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd105-stty.yaml`\n   - Status: SRD defined, waiting for implementation\n   - Will use `golang.org/x/sys/unix` for termios operations (available in go.mod)\n   - Key requirement: Match GNU stty byte-for-byte via differential testing\n\n2. **Related docs/specs**\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd052-tty.yaml` - tty command (already implemented)\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/docs/specs/use-cases/rel15.0-uc002-stty.yaml` - stty use case\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/docs/specs/use-cases/rel04.1-uc004-tty.yaml` - tty use case\n\n3. **Existing unix.* usage** (not termios, but illustrative):\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/df/main.go` - uses `unix.Statfs_t`, `unix.Getfsstat`, `unix.MNT_NOWAIT`, `unix.MNT_LOCAL`, `unix.Statfs`\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/test/main.go` - uses `golang.org/x/sys/unix`\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/touch/main.go` - uses `golang.org/x/sys/unix`\n\n4. **Existing terminal/ioctl usage** (close to termios):\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/pkg/sys/terminal.go`\n     - `unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(os.Stdout.Fd()), unix.TIOCGWINSZ)` - gets terminal width\n     - `IsTerminal(fd uintptr)` - checks if fd is a terminal\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/tty/main.go` - uses C.ttyname() via cgo\n\n---\n\n### Typical cmd/ Implementation Patterns\n\n#### Copyright Header (Mandatory)\nAll files start with:\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n```\n\n#### Help and Version Text\n- Defined as module-level constants: `const helpText = ...` and `const versionText = ...`\n- Help text is comprehensive multi-line strings with \"Usage: \" and detailed options\n- Version text is single line: `<tool> (go-unix-utils) dev`\n\nExample from `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/sort/main.go` (lines 17-46):\n```go\nconst helpText = `Usage: sort [OPTION]... [FILE]...\nWrite sorted concatenation of all FILE(s) to standard output.\n...\n```\n\n#### Flag Parsing Approach\nTwo patterns observed:\n\n1. **Simple flags (cat, tee, tty)**: Direct parseArgs + parseShortFlags functions\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/tty/main.go` (lines 56-103)\n   - Handles `--` for end-of-flags\n   - Processes long flags with `strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\")`\n   - Processes short flags recursively\n   - Returns values directly\n\n2. **Complex flags (md5sum)**: Options struct + parse functions\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/md5sum/main.go` (lines 54-117)\n   - Options struct holds all flags as fields\n   - `parseLongFlag()` and `parseShortFlags()` functions modify struct\n   - Returns `(options, []string)` tuple\n\n#### Exit Codes\n- Success: `os.Exit(0)` or no exit (implicit 0)\n- General error: `os.Exit(1)`\n- Usage/flag error: `os.Exit(2)` - used by tty for extra operands or unknown flags\n- SIGPIPE handling: Exit 0 (via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`)\n\n#### SIGPIPE Handling\n- Every cmd/ calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main()\n- Defined in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n- Alternative: `signal.Ignore(syscall.SIGPIPE)` (used in tee/main.go line 18)\n\n#### File Structure\nThree patterns observed:\n\n1. **Single-file cmd/** (~40-150 lines):\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/tty/main.go` (104 lines)\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/chronic/main.go` (89 lines)\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/tee/main.go` (153 lines)\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/md5sum/main.go` (117 lines)\n\n2. **Two-file cmd/** (main.go + test_test.go):\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/cat/main.go` (219 lines)\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/tee/main.go` + tee_test.go\n\n3. **Multi-file cmd/** (split by responsibility):\n   - `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/cmd/sort/` has 5 files:\n     - main.go (469 lines) - flag parsing, entry point\n     - check.go (60 lines) - check mode logic\n     - compare.go (174 lines) - comparison logic\n     - keys.go (276 lines) - key parsing\n     - sort_test.go (278 lines) - tests\n\n---\n\n### Documentation Constitutions and Style Guides\n\n**Location**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/docs/constitutions/`\n\nThree key constitution files:\n\n#### 1. **execution.yaml** - Stitch Phase Rules\nKey articles for implementation:\n- **E8 (Function size limit)**: No function may exceed **40 lines of code** (hard limit)\n  - Common seams: validation logic, formatting logic, I/O operations, branch-specific handling\n- **E9 (File size limit)**: Go source files should stay under **500 lines of production code**\n  - When exceeded, split by responsibility: main.go (entry point and arg parsing), format.go (output formatting), additional files as needed\n- **E10 (DRY enforcement)**: Duplication threshold is two - if you write the same logic twice, extract it\n\nOther key rules:\n- **E1**: Code must correspond to existing SRDs and architecture\n- **E2**: Commit messages must mention which SRDs are implemented\n- **E3**: No scope creep - don't modify files outside the task scope\n- **E5**: Every acceptance criterion must be verified\n- **E6**: Non-goals must not be implemented\n- **E7**: Skip ambiguous requirements entirely (don't partially implement)\n\n**Copyright header required** (lines 88-91):\n```\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n```\n\n#### 2. **design.yaml** - Documentation Standards\n- **Document types**: VISION, ARCHITECTURE, SRD, use case, test suite, engineering guideline, interface spec\n- **Naming conventions**:\n  - SRD: `srd[NNN]-[feature-name].yaml`\n  - Use case: `rel[NN].[N]-uc[NNN]-[short-name].yaml`\n  - Test suite: `test-rel[NN].[N]-[name].yaml`\n- **Traceability**: Every artifact traces through chain: vision → architecture → SRD → use case → test suite → code\n- **Forbidden documentation terms**: \"critical,\" \"key,\" \"deliberate,\" \"strategic,\" \"precisely,\" \"absolutely\"\n\n#### 3. **go-style.yaml** - Go Coding Standards\nKey patterns:\n- **Design patterns**: Strategy, Command, Facade, Factory, Decorator, Adapter\n- **Interfaces**: Introduce interface only when you have two concrete implementations\n- **Naming conventions**:\n  - Exported: `PascalCase` (e.g., `CupboardConfig`)\n  - Unexported: `camelCase` (e.g., `cobblerConfig`)\n  - CLI flags: `kebab-case` (e.g., `--silence-agent`)\n  - Factories: `New` prefix (e.g., `NewBackend()`)\n- **Implementation strategy**: Write all source files before running build/test; plan mentally first\n- **Standard packages**: mage, cobra, viper, testify, yaml.v3, encoding/json\n\n---\n\n### SRD Requirements for stty (srd105-stty.yaml)\n\nFrom `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd105-stty.yaml`:\n\n**Key Requirements:**\n- **R1**: Default display (no args prints summary)\n- **R2**: All settings display (`-a` or `--all`)\n- **R3**: Save/restore and device (`-g` for machine-readable, `-F DEVICE` for alternate device)\n- **R4**: Change settings (setting names as args, prefix with `-` to disable)\n- **R5**: Special characters (intr, quit, erase, kill, eof, eol, eol2, swtch, start, stop, susp, rprnt, werase, lnext, discard, min, time)\n- **R6**: Combination and speed settings (sane, cooked, raw, evenp, oddp, speed)\n- **R7**: Exit codes and SIGPIPE (exit 0 on success, exit 1 on error, handle SIGPIPE gracefully)\n\n**Non-goals:**\n- Does not implement all obscure termios flags; covers commonly used set matching GNU stty output\n\n**Package contract imports:**\n- `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n---\n\n### Related Dependencies and Modules\n\n- **go.mod**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/go.mod`\n  - Go 1.26.3\n  - Requires `golang.org/x/sys v0.45.0` (for unix.* types)\n  - Requires `golang.org/x/crypto v0.52.0`\n\n- **pkg/sys** (reusable utilities): `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5641/pkg/sys/`\n  - `terminal.go` - `TerminalWidth()`, `IsTerminal(fd)`\n  - `sigpipe.go` - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n  - `signal.go`, `fileinfo.go`, `stat_darwin.go` - other utilities"}]}]},"parent_tool_us